# .agent/ holds local notes, with three deliberate exceptions. The verification
# baselines are a GATE CRITERION, not a note: the failing-test-file set is what a
# commit is judged against, so it has to travel with the code instead of living
# on one machine. The retrieval follow-ups are DEFERRED WORK WITH EVIDENCE --
# decisions taken, with the reasoning that justified deferring them; "remembered
# by whoever was in the session" has already cost this project twice. The wiki
# plan is the same rule applied ahead of the work rather than after it: its
# locked premises were decided once, and a premise that lives only in a chat log
# gets re-argued from scratch by whoever builds against it. The canvas retrieval
# units are that rule again for work NOT YET DISPATCHED: each unit's decisions
# are reserved for a human and its costs were measured against the live
# database, so a later reader inherits the measurement instead of re-deriving
# it -- and instead of inheriting the wrong number from a chat log. The media
# sources unit is the same rule once more, and it carries something the others
# do not: CORRECTIONS TO ITS OWN EARLIER DRAFT, each with the schema or function
# that disproved it. A plan that was wrong once and is now right reads
# identically to a plan that was always right -- unless the disproof travels
# with it, which is how the "risk-free" stage stops being re-proposed.
# `.agent/*` rather than `.agent/` is what makes a negation possible at all --
# git will not descend into an ignored directory.
.agent/*
.claude/
!.agent/verification-baselines.md
!.agent/retrieval-followups.md
!.agent/wiki-plan.md
!.agent/canvas-retrieval-units.md
!.agent/media-sources-unit.md
!.agent/docx-extraction-assessment.md
!.agent/docx-live-acceptance.md

